# Backend Docker Build

## Strapi and `.strapi` in the image

Strapi creates a `.strapi` directory (cache/CLI state) during `strapi build`. Including this path in image layers can cause **containerd layer extraction failures** on some hosts:

- Error: `failed to extract layer ... UtimesNanoAt for .../fs/app/.strapi: no such file or directory`
- Cause: overlayfs/snapshotter tries to set timestamps on `app/.strapi`; due to layer ordering or filesystem quirks the path may not exist at that moment, so extraction fails.

## Required mitigations

1. **apps/backend/.dockerignore**  
   Must ignore:
   - `.strapi`
   - `.strapi-updater.json`
   - `.strapi-cloud.json`  
   So local Strapi artifacts are never sent as build context.

2. **Dockerfile (main.Dockerfile, dev.Dockerfile)**  
   After `strapi build`, remove Strapi cache dirs so they are not snapshotted into the layer or copied into the runner stage:
   ```dockerfile
   RUN pnpm run build \
       && rm -rf .strapi .cache .tmp
   ```
   Do not remove them only in a separate `RUN` if that would leave them in an earlier layer that is still extracted.

## “Stuck” after `✔ Building admin panel`

That message is the **last line Strapi prints**. If you never see `strapi build finished at …`, the **Node process has not exited** — not Docker going silent.

Common causes in this repo:

1. **`REST_CACHE_PROVIDER=redis` during build** — With `NODE_ENV=production`, `config/plugins.ts` defaults rest-cache to Redis. There is no Redis in the builder image; plugin init can block after the admin webpack step. **Fix:** builder stage sets `ENV REST_CACHE_PROVIDER=memory` (runtime deploy env still uses Redis).
2. **Webpack workers** — Admin build may leave watchers open. **Fix:** `src/admin/webpack.config.js` sets `watch: false`.
3. **Heap / GC thrashing** — Builder defaults `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=4096`; GitLab `ENABLE_LARGE_HEAP` defaults to `true` so CI passes the same unless overridden.

The Dockerfile splits `pnpm run build` and artifact cleanup into separate `RUN` layers so `#26 DONE` appears as soon as Strapi exits.

## NPM registry (build)

`main.Dockerfile` and `dev.Dockerfile` default `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` to the Abrha mirror, with Liara → Runflare → npmjs fallbacks (same chain as frontend/social).

Every builder-stage `pnpm` step uses `--mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/node/corepack`. That cache is **not** part of the builder image filesystem — do **not** `COPY --from=builder /root/.cache/node/corepack` into the runner. The runner stage runs `fallback-registry.sh … pnpm --version` once (no cache mount) so Corepack/pnpm land in the image layer, then copies to `/home/node/.cache/node/` for the `node` user at runtime.

Override at build time when needed:

```bash
docker build \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_URL="https://…" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL="https://package-mirror.liara.ir/repository/npm/" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_THIRD_FALLBACK_URL="https://mirror-npm.runflare.com/" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL="https://registry.npmjs.org/" \
  -f apps/backend/main.Dockerfile .
```

## Builder env (Strapi build)

| Variable | Builder value | Why |
|----------|---------------|-----|
| `REST_CACHE_PROVIDER` | `memory` | Avoid Redis connect hang during `strapi build` |
| `CI` | `true` | Webpack/CI-friendly admin build |
| `NODE_OPTIONS` | `--max-old-space-size=4096` (default) | Admin webpack memory |

Runtime Redis rest-cache comes from deploy `main.env` / `dev.env`, not from the builder `ENV`.

## Alpine APK fallback

The backend Dockerfiles install build/runtime native dependencies through `.cursor/docker/fallback-apk.sh`. The script first rewrites Alpine repositories to `https://mirror.arvancloud.ir/alpine`; if `apk add` fails, it restores the default Alpine repositories and retries once. This applies to:

- Builder: `build-base`, `python3`, `vips-dev`, `fftw-dev`
- Runner: `su-exec`, `vips`, `vips-dev` in `main.Dockerfile`; `vips`, `vips-dev` in `dev.Dockerfile`

## CI defaults

Dockerfile defaults apply only when **no** `--build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_URL` is passed. Pipelines override them:

- **GitLab** (`build:backend`): passes `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` and `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL`
- **GitHub Actions** (`backend-cicd.yml`): passes the same build args from secrets or repo defaults

If builds still hit another mirror, check the **`NPM_REGISTRY_URL`** and **`NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL`** CI/CD variables in GitLab/GitHub — they take precedence over repo defaults.

## Runtime

Strapi may create `.strapi` again at runtime; that is fine. The issue is only with the path being present in the built image layers and then extracted on the deployment host.
